So, I started this Neutral Human Monk a day before last christmas, 2005/12/23.
I decided to go illiterate to keep me entertained actually it worked.
It worked out really well, I kept those five or six magic markers on the
floor, didn't bother with dozens of spellbooks and myriads of scrolls.
I deactivated the mail function and I ignored engravings and tombstones.
I even managed to remember engrave-identifying wands with only the letter x.

There were a few shortcomings this game, though.
The only altars have been minetown and quest, for example. The next is the
total lack of any form of Magic Resistance or water crossing.
After evading Titan after Titan, Vampires (who had robes of protection)
and Liches, I somehow tricked One-Eyed Sam into selling me a pair of jumping
boots for some of my ~100k zorkmids.
Those were put to good use to cross Medusa and gain access to the next level,
the castle. Here I hoped to trade a wish or two for Magic Resistance and other
goodies.
With a bit of luck I took out all the Liches here and used Perseus' levitation
boots to go around the back of the castle. After hacking and slashing my way
through the crowd I first sorted through the loot and found something I find
myself looking for in every game I start... a T-Shirt!
I immediately read it for the nice fortune:

	I'm with stupid -->

The next turn I wished I had a pet to put this T-Shirt on to and put beside me.
What was the conduct I wanted to keep this game? And managed to keep up to this
point?
Correct, illiterate conduct.
So I got the WoW (which happened to be 0:3 even), stand in the middle of the
throne room in the castle and... #quit

